// The page header of the users table: the view half of the keyless
// `+Header#header` embed (user-list-header.ts is the behavior half, joined to
// it by the instance name). Keyless — no `key`, no `each` in the children
// entry — so the boundary hands it the page's whole state (there is nothing to
// slice: the header owns no data of its own), and its events leave prefixed
// `header.`, reaching its component alone. The "new user" button is the
// header's one concern; the page never sees its click.
header.ui-page-header
  h1.ui-page-title Users
  div.ui-page-actions
    button.new.ui-button.ui-button-default(@click=newUser) new user
